WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.541 --> 00:00:29.791


2
00:00:29.791 --> 00:00:34.291
<b>Here, Krishna is explaining </b>
<b>to Arjun what he must do.</b>

3
00:00:34.291 --> 00:00:36.041
<b>He says, </b>
<b>"Arjun,</b>

4
00:00:36.041 --> 00:00:39.500
<b>you have the right only to perform your duties,</b>

5
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.458
<b>but not to their outcomes.</b>

6
00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:44.958
<b>Neither should you be preoccupied </b>
<b>with the results of your actions,</b>

7
00:00:44.958 --> 00:00:49.458
<b>nor should you consider yourself</b>
<b>the cause of their consequences."</b>

8
00:00:54.291 --> 00:00:57.166
<b>Understand this through this dialogue,</b>

9
00:00:57.166 --> 00:00:59.250
<b>where Lord Krishna says:</b>

10
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.416
<b>"Arjun,</b>

11
00:01:00.416 --> 00:01:03.958
<b>your right extends only </b>
<b>to performing your actions.</b>

12
00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:07.083
<b>You have no claim over their results."</b>
<b>Arjun:</b>

13
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:08.333
<b>"But Krishna</b>

14
00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:10.208
<b>if I perform any action,</b>

15
00:01:10.208 --> 00:01:13.458
<b>it will surely lead to some outcome,</b>

16
00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:19.583
<b>and with that outcome will come either joy </b>
<b>or distress."Krishna:</b>

17
00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:20.583
<b>"Arjun,</b>

18
00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:26.625
<b>this joy or distress only exists when you </b>
<b>expect something from your actions,</b>

19
00:01:26.625 --> 00:01:29.000
<b>when you believe you have </b>
<b>control over the results,</b>

20
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.375
<b>when you think that outcome</b>
<b>came because of you.</b>

21
00:01:33.375 --> 00:01:35.416
<b>If you have no expectations from your actions,</b>

22
00:01:35.416 --> 00:01:37.541
<b>if you're not the cause of the results,</b>

23
00:01:37.541 --> 00:01:39.333
<b>if you have no claim over them</b>

24
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:43.291
<b>then where does the question of </b>
<b>joy or distress even arise?"Arjun:</b>

25
00:01:43.291 --> 00:01:44.625
<b>"But Krishna,</b>

26
00:01:44.625 --> 00:01:46.625
<b>if I have no expectations from my actions,</b>

27
00:01:46.625 --> 00:01:48.708
<b>if their results aren't because of me,</b>

28
00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:52.958
<b>if the joy or sorrow from </b>
<b>those results isn't mine either</b>

29
00:01:52.958 --> 00:01:56.208
<b>perhaps then it would be better not to act at all.</b>

30
00:01:56.208 --> 00:02:00.000
<b>At least I would remain free</b>
<b>from the bondage of karma." Krishna</b>

31
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.083
<b>"Arjun,</b>

32
00:02:01.083 --> 00:02:03.500
<b>abstaining from action is never appropriate.</b>

33
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.833
<b>I have explained this before</b>

34
00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:11.500
<b>if you neglect your duties, you will incur sin.</b>

35
00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.625
<b>You must fulfill your responsibilities,</b>

36
00:02:13.625 --> 00:02:16.000
<b>you must perform your actions.</b>

37
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.291
<b>The truth is,</b>

38
00:02:17.291 --> 00:02:22.083
<b>when you perform your duties </b>
<b>without any expectations,</b>

39
00:02:22.083 --> 00:02:27.791
<b>it will purify your mind and</b>
<b>lead to your spiritual growth.</b>

40
00:02:27.791 --> 00:02:28.875
<b>Therefore,</b>

41
00:02:28.875 --> 00:02:30.833
<b>you must act,</b>

42
00:02:30.833 --> 00:02:31.958
<b>but</b>

43
00:02:31.958 --> 00:02:35.375
<b>without any expectations whatsoever."</b>

44
00:02:40.166 --> 00:02:42.041
<b>What happens</b>

45
00:02:42.041 --> 00:02:47.458
<b>when you dream of achieving</b>
<b>something significant in life</b>

46
00:02:47.458 --> 00:02:51.750
<b>and begin working towards it?</b>

47
00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:58.041
<b>Typically, you start constantly </b>
<b>expecting results.</b>

48
00:02:58.041 --> 00:02:59.166
<b>And</b>

49
00:02:59.166 --> 00:03:02.666
<b>after that?</b>

50
00:03:02.666 --> 00:03:07.166
<b>If you succeed and that dream is fulfilled,</b>

51
00:03:07.166 --> 00:03:10.500
<b>you experience extraordinary joy.</b>

52
00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:15.750
<b>Sometimes, people even become </b>
<b>arrogant and proud in such situations.</b>

53
00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:20.625
<b>They feel that since they've achieved </b>
<b>such an extraordinary goal, </b>

54
00:03:20.625 --> 00:03:24.500
<b>they themselves must be extraordinary.</b>

55
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.125
<b>But if</b>

56
00:03:26.125 --> 00:03:30.500
<b>failure comes instead, extreme </b>
<b>disappointment follows.</b>

57
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:34.208
<b>You begin to doubt your capabilities.</b>

58
00:03:34.208 --> 00:03:37.833
<b>The pain of a broken dream sets in.</b>

59
00:03:37.833 --> 00:03:42.291
<b>Neither of these mental states is healthy</b>

60
00:03:42.291 --> 00:03:49.208
<b>neither excessive elation nor extreme despair.</b>

61
00:03:49.208 --> 00:03:53.208
<b>One leads you toward ego,</b>

62
00:03:53.208 --> 00:03:57.375
<b>the other toward self-deprecation.</b>

63
00:03:57.375 --> 00:03:58.375
<b>Perhaps</b>

64
00:03:58.375 --> 00:04:02.375
<b>you'll say that you don't have ego,</b>

65
00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:08.000
<b>that you only believe in self-confidence.</b>

66
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.666
<b>Understand it this way</b>

67
00:04:10.666 --> 00:04:15.916
<b>if self-confidence is tied to </b>
<b>expecting a particular outcome,</b>

68
00:04:15.916 --> 00:04:22.291
<b>then somewhere you believe you </b>
<b>have control over that outcome. </b>

69
00:04:22.291 --> 00:04:28.791
<b>But do you really have sole</b>
<b>control over that result?</b>

70
00:04:28.791 --> 00:04:31.291
<b>If the goal was so significant,</b>

71
00:04:31.291 --> 00:04:38.416
<b>didn't other circumstances</b>
<b>and people play a part?</b>

72
00:04:38.416 --> 00:04:42.458
<b>If you look carefully, you'll realize</b>

73
00:04:42.458 --> 00:04:50.500
<b>that such a big dream couldn't have been </b>
<b>fulfilled without many other forms of support.</b>

74
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:54.166
<b>The true definition of self-confidence isn't</b>

75
00:04:54.166 --> 00:04:55.000
<b>"Yes,</b>

76
00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.041
<b>I will definitely achieve this goal."</b>

77
00:04:59.041 --> 00:05:02.583
<b>The true definition is</b>

78
00:05:02.583 --> 00:05:03.791
<b>"Yes,</b>

79
00:05:03.791 --> 00:05:05.000
<b>I know</b>

80
00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:09.250
<b>I will perform my duties completely."</b>

81
00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:10.125
<b>Here,</b>

82
00:05:10.125 --> 00:05:17.416
<b> you're only assured about </b>
<b>your actions, not the results.</b>

83
00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:22.375
<b>This mindset will teach</b>
<b>you gratitude in success,</b>

84
00:05:22.375 --> 00:05:24.083
<b>protecting you from ego.</b>

85
00:05:24.083 --> 00:05:25.458
<b>Similarly,</b>

86
00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:32.500
<b>this thinking will shield you from the </b>
<b>sorrow and depression of failure,</b>

87
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:33.291
<b> because</b>

88
00:05:33.291 --> 00:05:34.916
<b>you're assured</b>

89
00:05:34.916 --> 00:05:38.875
<b>that you fulfilled your duty completely.</b>

90
00:05:38.875 --> 00:05:41.833
<b>There was no lacking in you;</b>

91
00:05:41.833 --> 00:05:42.666
<b>perhaps</b>

92
00:05:42.666 --> 00:05:48.000
<b>circumstances simply weren't </b>
<b>favorable this time.</b>

93
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:50.416
<b>Gratitude in success,</b>

94
00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:52.458
<b>patience in failure</b>

95
00:05:52.458 --> 00:05:56.208
<b>this is a powerful mantra for inner peace.</b>

96
00:06:01.458 --> 00:06:04.500
<b>You have control only over your actions,</b>

97
00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.250
<b>not their results.</b>

98
00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:16.041
<b>This perspective is crucial and </b>
<b>helpful in family and social environments.</b>

99
00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:19.291
<b>You can see this in two ways.</b>

100
00:06:19.291 --> 00:06:20.375
<b>First</b>

101
00:06:20.375 --> 00:06:24.541
<b>any significant result comes from </b>
<b>many people's contributions.</b>

102
00:06:24.541 --> 00:06:27.000
<b>If the outcome is successful,</b>

103
00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.583
<b>you know that</b>

104
00:06:28.583 --> 00:06:32.875
<b>you don't have sole claim to this result.</b>

105
00:06:32.875 --> 00:06:37.541
<b>Many people, big and small, have contributed,</b>

106
00:06:37.541 --> 00:06:42.083
<b>and because they too </b>
<b>have a hand in this outcome, </b>

107
00:06:42.083 --> 00:06:46.083
<b>your gratitude towards them will grow.</b>

108
00:06:46.083 --> 00:06:52.625
<b>Being grateful strengthens both</b>
<b>social and family relationships.</b>

109
00:06:52.625 --> 00:06:53.750
<b>Conversely,</b>

110
00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.750
<b>if the result is unsuccessful,</b>

111
00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:00.750
<b>just as you aren't the cause of that failure,</b>

112
00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:05.791
<b>neither is anyone else</b>

113
00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:08.958
<b>circumstances were simply unfavourable.</b>

114
00:07:08.958 --> 00:07:10.000
<b>In such situations,</b>

115
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:15.291
<b>your patience with others will </b>
<b>certainly have a positive impact.</b>

116
00:07:15.291 --> 00:07:20.083
<b>Now understand this teaching in another way.</b>

117
00:07:20.083 --> 00:07:26.750
<b>Often, we help our family members</b>
<b>or loved ones,</b>

118
00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:30.250
<b>give them work-related advice,</b>

119
00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:34.833
<b>or suggest some changes in their lives.</b>

120
00:07:34.833 --> 00:07:35.833
<b>But</b>

121
00:07:35.833 --> 00:07:40.958
<b> if no change appears despite our many efforts,</b>

122
00:07:40.958 --> 00:07:43.916
<b>we become discouraged.</b>

123
00:07:43.916 --> 00:07:47.250
<b>We distance ourselves from that person,</b>

124
00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:50.958
<b>thinking it's completely pointless to help them.</b>

125
00:07:50.958 --> 00:07:51.791
<b>Perhaps</b>

126
00:07:51.791 --> 00:07:57.333
<b>we mentally label them as "incapable."</b>

127
00:07:57.333 --> 00:08:05.125
<b>And such negative feelings </b>
<b>can only harm relationships.</b>

128
00:08:05.125 --> 00:08:07.041
<b>We must realize</b>

129
00:08:07.041 --> 00:08:13.833
<b>that just as we don't have complete</b>
<b>control over any outcome,</b>

130
00:08:13.833 --> 00:08:14.875
<b>perhaps</b>

131
00:08:14.875 --> 00:08:18.416
<b>they too face difficult circumstances</b>

132
00:08:18.416 --> 00:08:25.750
<b>or mental struggles that prevent their success.</b>

133
00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:29.291
<b>This understanding will awaken empathy in us.</b>

134
00:08:29.291 --> 00:08:34.333
<b>It will motivate us to continue our support.</b>

135
00:08:34.333 --> 00:08:38.291
<b>And this nature will strengthen relationships.</b>

136
00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:47.250
<b>"Having no expectation of results"</b>

137
00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.541
<b>In a professional environment.,</b>

138
00:08:49.541 --> 00:08:57.208
<b>there's a major misconception of understanding </b>
<b>this as aimlessness or carelessness.</b>

139
00:08:57.208 --> 00:08:59.000
<b>Carelessness</b>

140
00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:01.000
<b>we must understand</b>

141
00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:06.666
<b>that the word 'carelessness' </b>
<b>relates only to action.</b>

142
00:09:06.666 --> 00:09:12.208
<b>It means not being mindful of your duties.</b>

143
00:09:12.208 --> 00:09:14.916
<b>Avoiding work.</b>

144
00:09:14.916 --> 00:09:16.208
<b>But</b>

145
00:09:16.208 --> 00:09:20.041
<b>if someone performs their duties completely,</b>

146
00:09:20.041 --> 00:09:24.208
<b>only without expecting results,</b>

147
00:09:24.208 --> 00:09:28.750
<b>they are definitely not careless.</b>

148
00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:31.250
<b>Similarly, aimlessness</b>

149
00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:35.125
<b>this means having no goal at all.</b>

150
00:09:35.125 --> 00:09:36.416
<b>It's not that</b>

151
00:09:36.416 --> 00:09:43.041
<b>someone who doesn't</b>
<b>expect results has no goals.</b>

152
00:09:43.041 --> 00:09:49.666
<b>A person mindful of their duties is indeed </b>
<b>progressing toward a goal,</b>

153
00:09:49.666 --> 00:09:53.333
<b>working in that direction.</b>

154
00:09:53.333 --> 00:09:56.416
<b>The only difference is that</b>

155
00:09:56.416 --> 00:10:02.041
<b>upon achieving a goal, they don't </b>
<b>consider themselves the primary cause,</b>

156
00:10:02.041 --> 00:10:05.916
<b>nor do they declare it as such.</b>

157
00:10:05.916 --> 00:10:13.916
<b>They remain grateful </b>
<b>to circumstances, to others' help.</b>

158
00:10:13.916 --> 00:10:16.666
<b>And when results are unfavourable,</b>

159
00:10:16.666 --> 00:10:21.375
<b>they neither blame others </b>
<b>nor become discouraged.</b>

160
00:10:21.375 --> 00:10:28.958
<b>Such a person views both good and bad </b>
<b>results in a balanced way.</b>

161
00:10:28.958 --> 00:10:34.833
<b>They neither waste excessive time </b>
<b>in elation nor in despair.</b>

162
00:10:34.833 --> 00:10:43.083
<b>After any result, they immediately engage in </b>
<b>their work once again.</b>

163
00:10:43.083 --> 00:10:46.708
<b>"Having no expectation of results"</b>

164
00:10:46.708 --> 00:10:53.041
<b>don't make the mistake of understanding</b>
<b>this as aimlessness or carelessness.</b>

